      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALTA SIERRA (8) led for most of the trip when scoring by a neck over 1720m at Penrith last start. He has a tough draw to overcome but back in winning form should be fighting out the finish. DOUBLE FEAR (1) finished third here last start over 2300m when after he showed good gate speed raced in behind the lead for most of the trip. He has placed third in three of his last four starts and from the pole draw rates well as a leading chance. DOM TORETTO NZ (5) finished a neck second at long odds over 2300m here last start when trying to lead all of the way. Dropping back in distance could prove hard to catch. OAKIE SMOKESHOW (2) finished fourth here last start over today's distance after he raced in behind the leader for most of the trip. He has recorded five of his six career wins at this track. From his handy draw should get a soft trip in the running and rates well as an each-way chance.",
